Interpretation:
  n_used    : classes with n > 100 predictions (must be ≥ 3 for usable taxonomy)
  C2%       : share of bars predicted as range — lower = more trends captured
  ΔP(up)    : direction-predictability spread — higher = better discrimination
  ΔE[fwd]   : forward magnitude spread — higher = bigger per-regime distinction
  ΔTP%/ΔSL% : barrier-outcome spread — directly relevant to trading
  WSNR      : weighted avg signal-to-noise — overall signal strength

  IDEAL: low C2% + high ΔP(up) + high ΔE[fwd] + high WSNR
  TRADE-OFF: lowering C2% may reduce per-class signal (lower SNR)
